lookup={x['id']:x for x in src}
scope='This guide covers NCCP00353 osimertinib on its own: T790M-positive advanced disease, first-line activating-EGFR advanced disease, or completely resected stage IB–IIIA Ex19del/L858R adjuvant treatment. The newer licensed post-chemoradiation setting and osimertinib with platinum/pemetrexed need their own applicable plan; their study results and support medicines are not added to this monotherapy suite.'
purpose='Osimertinib blocks abnormal EGFR growth signals in selected lung cancers. After complete surgery, treatment aims to lower the risk of cancer returning. In advanced cancer, it aims to control cancer and delay progression. Confirm which aim applies to you.'
schedule='The usual starting dose is 80 mg by mouth once daily, every day without a planned rest week. Use the dose on your prescription. Advanced treatment continues while helping and tolerated; adjuvant treatment is planned for up to three years, with earlier stopping if cancer returns or side effects become unacceptable.'
admin='Take at the same time each day, with or without food. Swallow whole with water; do not crush, split or chew. If you forget a dose, take it when remembered unless less than 12 hours remain before the next dose, when it should be skipped. Confirm the instruction with your pharmacist if the next dose is exactly 12 hours away. Do not take an extra dose without advice if you vomit. Ask for the approved water-dispersion instructions if swallowing is difficult.'
baseline=['Confirm the relevant EGFR test, treatment setting and prescription. Adjuvant treatment needs complete resection and the specific stage/mutation criteria.','Blood count, kidney, liver and bone profile; ECG before treatment.','Consider an echocardiogram or MUGA LVEF assessment for cardiac risks or symptoms; review all medicines, pregnancy, contraception and breastfeeding.']
ongoing=['Repeat blood count, kidney, liver and bone profile at the agreed reviews; extra checks may be needed for symptoms or abnormal results.','NCCP specifies ECG at baseline and cycle 2, then cycle 3 onwards if clinically indicated. The team translates cycle 2 into a booked review; the tablets remain daily, without a treatment break.','LVEF assessment if clinically indicated; ECG and electrolytes with cardiac/QT risks. Scans and disease checks follow the Consultant plan.']
urgent='Contact the oncology team urgently for new or worsening breathlessness, cough or fever; fainting, palpitations or chest pain; blistering/peeling skin or mouth/eye/genital sores; unusual bruising, bleeding or marked pallor; severe diarrhoea, dehydration or inability to drink. New eye pain, light sensitivity or blurred vision needs prompt advice. Severe breathing difficulty, collapse or swelling of the tongue/throat needs emergency help. Use your unit’s temperature and 24-hour contact instructions.'
repro='Avoid pregnancy during treatment. Effective contraception continues for at least two months after the final dose for women and four months for men. Osimertinib may reduce hormonal contraceptive effectiveness; discuss a suitable method. Do not breastfeed during treatment. Discuss fertility and plans for pregnancy before starting.'
mechanism='Osimertinib is an EGFR tyrosine kinase inhibitor. It blocks signalling from sensitising EGFR mutations and the T790M resistance mutation, reducing cancer-cell growth signals. The tumour test and treatment setting determine whether it is appropriate.'
support=[{'title':'Skin and nails','text':'Agree an EGFR-inhibitor skin-care plan from the start and report rash or painful nail changes early. Blistering, peeling or mucosal sores need urgent assessment.','source_ids':['nccp','smpc']},{'title':'Bowel symptoms and hydration','text':'Report diarrhoea early, follow the prescribed symptom plan and maintain fluids if able. Severe diarrhoea, weakness or reduced urine needs urgent advice.','source_ids':['smpc']},{'title':'Nausea medicines','text':'Osimertinib has minimal-to-low oral emetic risk. Routine infusion premedication is not usually needed. Agree rescue medicines individually, including QT and interaction review; do not copy a chemotherapy antiemetic course.','source_ids':['nccp','smpc','antiemetic']},{'title':'Medicine interactions','text':'Tell the team about all medicines and supplements. Do not take St John’s wort. Strong enzyme-inducing medicines and medicines that affect heart rhythm require pharmacy review before changes.','source_ids':['nccp','smpc']},{'title':'Pregnancy, fertility and breastfeeding','text':repro,'source_ids':['nccp','smpc']}]
interpret='The evidence differs by setting. In a study after complete surgery, adjuvant osimertinib improved survival compared with placebo. In untreated advanced EGFR-mutated cancer, it improved survival compared with older EGFR tablets. After resistance with T790M, it delayed progression compared with platinum/pemetrexed, but the final overall-survival comparison was not statistically significant. These results describe selected study groups and cannot predict your own outcome.'
